# ~/.config/agentbox/files — host files copied into the container, one per line.
#
# Each line is either:
#   <path>          copy host <path> -> the SAME <path> in the container
#   <src> <dst>     copy host <src> -> container <dst>
# A leading ~ is $HOME on the host and /home/agentbox in the container, so the one-token form
# works for anything under your home dir. Files keep their source mode and are chown'd to the
# agentbox user, so an SSH private key (mode 600) is usable as-is. `#` starts a comment.
#
# Example: copy a non-default SSH key into the container under the name ssh discovers by
# default, so a script can reach a host service exposed via a forwarded port (see `ports`).
# Substitute your own key name on the left:
~/.ssh/mac-key ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
